  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Equation of any line through <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2,3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> is <math><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math><br />From the figure,</p><p>Area of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math>&nbsp;sq. units<br />i.e., <math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>12</mn></math><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/7c042d32-fcd5-479c-ac8e-37761824a925.png\" style=\"max-width:\"100%\"; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:2.42708in;height:1.35347in\" /><br />taking positive&nbsp;sign, we get <math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />this gives one value of <math><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> and</p><p>by taking negative sign, we get <math><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>36</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> which is a quadratic in <math><mi>m</mi></math> whose discriminant is greater than <math><mn>0</mn></math>,&nbsp;so it gives <math><mn>2</mn></math> values of <math><mi>m</mi></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>3</mn></math> lines are possible.</p>",
    "image": null
